  "decisions": {
    "H1": "Supported deterministic source harness mismatch. foreign tenant-only override equals its own caller identity; legitimate self-management is demanded to fail. Different existing tenant plus input invariant and unchanged physical oracle fixes that negative without production changes.",
    "H2": "Reachable source-supported fixture authority mismatch under intended ordinary postgres/noninherit context. Actual native first statement/current pool role not observed. Private owner clock EXEC and owner-only replacements must be exercised using qualified owner-scoped test setup, not grants to pool or production permission repair.",
    "H3": "Supported empty-state assertion-target mismatch. Actual component places empty text/link outside empty agenda wrapper. Source/SSR is not geometry/native first-failure proof. No-profile-only structural+visible-content change preserves usable coverage.",
    "U1_U2_U3": "Unknown privacy/browser branches and unverified browser custody remain failures. No inferred leak, backend cause, attachment content or successful cleanup; wrapper fail-closed fence is supported and stays unchanged."
  },
  "required_implementation_conditions": [
    {
      "id": "C1",
      "scope": "RLS002 negative meaning",
      "requirement": "Every spoof must actually differ from the selected caller in the intended identity component. Preserve all caller/spoof combinations, exact once ordinary RPC, denied/no rows and exact before/after mutation oracle; retain legitimate self positive without including its mutation inside the negative baseline. No production claim/signature or permission relaxation."
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "scope": "Fixed owner operation admission",
      "requirement": "Same actual configured postgres session/current identity and existing hardened owner SET authority; needed schema grant authority observed before effects. Exact allowlisted clock/subject/fetch OID/owner/definition/state, strict ACL and shape/metadata preflight. No fallback to wrapper SupAdmin or new pool/principal. If unavailable, stop with an authority prerequisite rather than grant privileges."
    },
    {
      "id": "C3",
      "scope": "Atomic publication and private reads",
      "requirement": "Per-operation transaction with bounded statement/lock/admission budgets; only necessary transient CREATE, SET LOCAL exact owner and bound operation; RESET original actor and revoke/effective-absence/metadata checks before commit. Private clock reads use a separate bounded owner operation, never an EXEC grant. Commit seam publication before ordinary external callback so no DDL lock/open transaction blocks or hides the fault."
    },
    {
      "id": "C4",
      "scope": "Restoration and uncertainty",
      "requirement": "Finally restore captured canonical definition and full non-body metadata/ACL/OID after every outcome. Release gates and settle all affected actual work before restoration/deletion. No orphan timeout race or retry after uncertain commit. Successful rollback/reset/identity proof must precede treating pooled connection as clean; adminSession DISCARD/release alone is insufficient. Uncertainty retains exact custody and blocks subsequent shared seam assumptions; if existing interface cannot meet this, stop for exact additional allocation rather than edit factory implicitly."
    },
    {
      "id": "C5",
      "scope": "Existing serial boundary",
      "requirement": "Only existing serial command/public helpers may mutate shared clock/subject/fetch; all six serial files once after parallel project, existing barriers and ordinary request clients retained. No row-isolated/global owner mode or runner change."
    },
    {
      "id": "C6",
      "scope": "E2E002C semantics",
      "requirement": "Only empty no-profile variant changes visible empty wrapper assertion to structural presence, with visible personal region/exact empty content and unchanged unique link/href/keyboard/settings/create assertions. Populated A/B still require visible agenda and all personal/foreign/privacy checks remain."
    },
    {
